 "tier1Summary": "Serbia's students took power at the ballot box: the [[p:Student List]] won an outright majority, ending more than a decade of [[p:Aleksandar Vučić]]'s dominance. Brussels set roadmaps for its four front-runners, though Hungary still holds up Ukraine's next talks. [[p:Donald Trump]]'s hint at a Russia deal covering \"all of Europe\" drew a sharp no from the EU. Beijing confirmed talks on a three-way summit with Trump and Putin.\n\nAt home, France's budget collapsed amid mass strikes. Poland's top court is split between rival leaderships, Sweden edges toward a government, and Spain votes on 29 Nov.\n\nIn the Gulf, the US launched a task force against Iran's land trade, and the [[p:Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps|IRGC]] lifted its missile-range cap. Houthi missiles damaged a Riyadh tower.",
